Z||000000||kornholio||10-10-1999||11:07 AM||||what happens if the diagnostic computer says I need to replace my EGR valve and I ignore it? The check engine light only comes on at around 6 am when I'm half way to work. When I get off work, the light is gone and it never turns back on. Would I not be able to drive the car if I don't replace it? How do you replace it? Is there a certain way, or should I leave it to the mechanic? The Haynes manual doesn't have any instructions for replacing it. Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||kornholio||10-10-1999||11:36 AM||||Oh, I just found the instructions for replacing the EGR valve.  4 lines of instructions. It sounds simple enough!||||reg||14
Z||000002||kornholio||10-10-1999||04:48 PM||||Does anyone know the original valve part number for my Fiero?  It is an 86 automatic V6 SE. I need the number to match it up with the correct orifice washer. This EGR valve came with about 10 different size washers.||||reg||5
Z||000003||batboy||10-10-1999||07:59 PM||||The part number may be on the old EGR or you can probably get it by calling a local Pontiac dealership. Also, since you have the V6, make sure you don't have a cracked EGR tube which is a fairly common problem.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Patrick||10-10-1999||08:15 PM||||<BR>When I replaced the EGR on my 4-banger, I had the same problem as korn has now. The EGR had already been replaced with an aftermarket one, so I couldn't get the original part number off of it. As usual, the local Pontiac dealership was less than helpful. They could only supply the current part number which was useless for my purposes.<P>I eventually emailed the manufacturer of the replacement EGR and they supplied me with the necessary information.||||reg||4
Z||000005||kornholio||10-10-1999||08:16 PM||||I won't have to worry about the EGR tube for a while. I had to replace it when it broke (yes broke, not cracked!) 2 months ago. It happened on the highway. I realized something was wrong when I let my foot off the gas and the car slowed down to 80 km/h and stopped there like I was using cruise control (I don't even have cruise). That scared the crap out of me.||||reg||1
